config STRATAFS_FS
	bool "StrataFS layered directory filesystem"
	depends on SECURITY_PKM
	select FS_STACK
	help
	  StrataFS presents an ordered set of independently managed directories
	  as one live merged tree.  It is the Peios Linux-compatibility filesystem
	  specified by PSD-011.

	  If unsure, say N.

config STRATAFS_FS_TEST_HOOKS
	bool "StrataFS test rendezvous and fail points"
	depends on STRATAFS_FS && SECURITYFS
	help
	  Compile in the securityfs hooks conformance tests use to hold a
	  copy-up open mid-flight or fail an internal step of one syscall
	  — windows no arrangement of real filesystems can produce.
	  (securityfs, not debugfs: kernel lockdown in integrity mode
	  refuses debugfs opens, and this kernel forces that mode.)

	  The hooks are doubly gated: even when built, nothing registers
	  and every hook site reduces to reading one never-true bool
	  unless the kernel is booted with stratafs.test_hooks=1. Only a
	  caller that can reach a mounted securityfs can then arm them.

	  If unsure, say N.

config STRATAFS_KUNIT_TEST
	bool "StrataFS KUnit tests"
	depends on STRATAFS_FS && KUNIT
	default SECURITY_PKM_KUNIT
	help
	  Exercise StrataFS mount parsing and bounded policy glue in-kernel.
